window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>Michael Kingman thought he was going to die by the executioner’s axe, forever labeled as a traitor. Still alive, and under the protection of the Orbis Mercenary company, Michael and his family and friends are deeply involved in the seemingly rival conspiracies that are tearing The Hollows apart. With the death of the King, both the Corrupt Prince and his sister Serena are vying for the throne, while the Rebel Emperor is spreading lies amongst the people, and all of them want Michael dead. This is a story of betrayal, murder, and rebellion, and in this direct sequel to the debut novel The Kingdom of Liars, also some hope for justice.</p> <p>For listeners who love the intrigue and widening scope of epic fantasy like Brandon Sanderson’s Mistborn and Brent Weeks’s The Black Prism, you will find your next must-listen fantasy series in The Legacy of the Mercenary King.</p> <p>Adapted from the novel and produced with a full cast of actors, immersive sound effects and cinematic music!</p> <p>Performed by Nick J. Russo as Michael, Carolyn Kashner as Serena, Keith Richards as Dark, Laura C. Harris as Naomi, Zeke Alton as Trey and Nora Achrati as Dawn. With additional performances by Amanda Forstrom, Bradley Foster Smith, Chris Davenport, Chris Stinson, Christopher Graybill, Christopher Walker, Colleen Delany, Crystal Lee, Daniel Llaca, David Cui Cui, Drew Kopas, Elena Anderson, Dawn Ursula, Eric Messner, Eva Wilhelm, Gabriel Michael, Gail Shalan, Ian Putnam, Joel David Santner, Jonathan David Bullock, Julienne Irons, K’lai Rivera, Keith Richards, Ken Jackson, Lise Bruneau, Lydia Kraniotis, Matthew Pauli, Michael Glenn, Morgan Dalla Betta, Nanette Savard, Natalie Van Sistine, Rayner Gabriel, Richard Rohan, Rob McFadyen, Samantha Cooper, Scott McCormick, Stephanie Nemeth-Parker, Steve Wannall, Steven Carpenter, Tanja Milojevic, Todd Scofield, Wyn Delano, Yasmin Tauzon and Zeke Alton.</p>"; 
